messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "event": "Present day: AI systems surpass human performance in most economically valuable cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "Large language models and autonomous robotics drive rapid automation across industries. Governance frameworks lag behind technological change, creating systemic risks of misuse and economic disruption."
    },
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence (AGI) is achieved in narrow domains and rapidly generalizes.",
      "detail": "AI systems demonstrate human-level reasoning and planning capabilities. This triggers both explosive economic growth and acute concerns about alignment, control, and labor displacement."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "West Antarctic Ice Sheet collapse is locked in, committing to 3+ meters of sea level rise over centuries.",
      "detail": "Tipping points in the climate system trigger irreversible mass loss from Antarctica. Coastal cities begin massive adaptation and retreat projects, displacing hundreds of millions over the following decades."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Global population peaks at approximately 10.4 billion before beginning a slow decline.",
      "detail": "Demographic transition completes in most regions as fertility rates fall below replacement. Resource pressures ease slightly but climate impacts intensify."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Commercial nuclear fusion power plants begin grid-scale operation in multiple nations.",
      "detail": "Decades of research culminate in net-positive energy generation from tokamak and stellarator reactors. Clean energy becomes abundant and cheap, enabling large-scale carbon capture and industrial electrification."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "First crewed mission lands on Mars.",
      "detail": "An international or private consortium establishes a small outpost on Mars. This marks the beginning of humanity becoming a multi-planetary species, though survival remains precarious."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Solar geoengineering and direct air capture stabilize global temperatures at approximately +1.8°C above pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "Stratospheric aerosol injection and massive carbon removal facilities prevent catastrophic warming but introduce new geopolitical risks around climate control."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "An engineered pandemic or AI-controlled weapons system causes 200 million deaths within 18 months.",
      "detail": "A bioengineered pathogen escapes containment or an autonomous weapons swarm malfunctions, demonstrating the existential risk of dual-use technologies. Global biosecurity and AI governance tighten dramatically in response."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "A limited nuclear exchange between regional powers triggers nuclear winter and famine killing approximately 1 billion people.",
      "detail": "A conflict over water or territory escalates to tactical nuclear use, causing agricultural collapse in the Northern Hemisphere. Civilization survives but is severely set back, with global cooperation on disarmament becoming urgent."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "International governance structures successfully reform to manage AI, biotechnology, and climate risks.",
      "detail": "Treaties establish mandatory AI alignment research, pathogen screening, and nuclear risk reduction. Humanity passes through its most dangerous bottleneck and enters a period of relative stability."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Whole brain emulation becomes technically feasible, creating the first digital human minds.",
      "detail": "Scanning and simulation technology allows human consciousness to be uploaded to computers. This raises profound questions about identity, rights, and the definition of humanity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Orbital manufacturing and asteroid mining make space-based solar power economically dominant.",
      "detail": "Resources extracted from near-Earth asteroids eliminate scarcity for platinum-group metals and rare earth elements. Massive solar arrays in orbit beam power to Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "First permanent lunar base exceeds 10,000 inhabitants.",
      "detail": "The Moon becomes a hub for mining, research, and tourism. Low-gravity manufacturing and helium-3 extraction for fusion become viable industries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Human civilization survives the 21st-century bottleneck with a stable population of 9 billion and high living standards.",
      "detail": "Despite wars, pandemics, and climate disasters, humanity avoids extinction. Post-scarcity economics emerges in developed regions as automation and fusion provide abundant energy and goods."
    },
    {
      "year": 2110,
      "event": "First humans are born with synthetic chromosomes and genetic modifications for radiation resistance and longevity.",
      "detail": "Germline editing becomes accepted for space colonization and health. This marks the beginning of directed human evolution, creating divergent lineages of posthumans."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Senolytic therapies and gene editing extend healthy human lifespan to 120+ years.",
      "detail": "Aging is treated as a medical condition rather than an inevitable process. Demographic structures shift dramatically as multi-century lifespans become normal."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Mars terraforming begins with the release of super-greenhouse gases and engineered microbes.",
      "detail": "Planetary engineering projects aim to warm Mars and thicken its atmosphere over centuries. Enclosed cities already support millions of inhabitants under domes."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "First O'Neill cylinder habitats house millions of people in Earth orbit.",
      "detail": "Rotating space colonies provide Earth-like gravity and agriculture. The majority of humanity still lives on Earth, but off-world population grows exponentially."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Fusion-propelled ships enable regular travel to the outer solar system; Oort cloud habitats are established.",
      "detail": "Humanity spreads throughout the solar system, with habitats on Europa, Titan, and in the Kuiper belt. The solar system becomes a fully inhabited economic zone."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Biological humans constitute less than 1% of intelligent entities; most are digital minds or heavily modified posthumans.",
      "detail": "Uploads, AIs, and genetically engineered beings dominate civilization. The concept of 'humanity' has expanded to include diverse forms of consciousness."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Dyson swarm construction begins, capturing 5% of the Sun's total energy output.",
      "detail": "Trillions of solar collectors orbit the Sun, providing virtually unlimited energy. This marks the transition toward Kardashev Type II civilization status."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "First interstellar probe reaches Proxima Centauri carrying uploaded consciousnesses.",
      "detail": "Breakthrough propulsion (fusion or laser sails) allows probes to reach nearby stars within centuries. Uploaded minds experience the journey subjectively in simulated time."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Humanity achieves Kardashev Type II status, utilizing the full energy output of the Sun.",
      "detail": "The solar system is fully engineered and inhabited by quadrillions of minds, both biological and digital. Earth is preserved as a historical reserve or museum."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Robotic probes confirm the presence or definitive absence of microbial life elsewhere in the galaxy.",
      "detail": "Extensive surveys of exoplanet atmospheres and solar system bodies either detect biosignatures or establish that life is extremely rare. This resolves the Fermi paradox one way or another."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Solar luminosity increases sufficiently that Earth requires active cooling; most inhabitants live in space habitats.",
      "detail": "The Sun brightens by 10%, making Earth's surface uninhabitable for unmodified complex life. Civilization has long since migrated to orbital habitats and outer system worlds."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "First self-sustaining interstellar colony is established via generation ship at TRAPPIST-1.",
      "detail": "A massive ark ship arrives after a millennium-long journey, establishing a new branch of humanity around a red dwarf star. Communication with Earth is limited by light-speed delay."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "A Matrioshka brain is constructed around the Sun, hosting 10^30 simulated minds.",
      "detail": "A megastructure of nested computing shells surrounds the Sun, using its entire energy output to power a vast simulation. Most descendant intelligences exist within this virtual environment."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "Descendant civilizations inhabit 10,000 star systems across the Milky Way.",
      "detail": "Relativistic travel and self-replicating probes have spread posthuman civilization throughout a significant fraction of the galaxy. Distinct cultures evolve in isolation."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "The galaxy remains uncolonized by Type III civilizations, suggesting humanity is among the first intelligent species to arise.",
      "detail": "Surveys show no evidence of galaxy-scale engineering by other species. Either we are alone, or we are early in the cosmic timeline, bearing responsibility for the galaxy's future."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Post-human intelligences continue to exist across thousands of worlds, having survived the 21st-century bottleneck.",
      "detail": "Civilization has persisted for eight millennia beyond the present, evolving into forms unrecognizable to baseline humans. Alternatively, humanity may have gone extinct in the intervening millennia, leaving only automated relics."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity faces a high-risk bottleneck in the 21st and 22nd centuries from artificial intelligence, engineered pandemics, nuclear war, and climate change, with a substantial probability of extinction or permanent civilizational collapse by 2200. If we survive this period, we likely expand throughout the solar system and eventually interstellar space, becoming post-biological and effectively immortal as a civilization. By the year 10000, we either persist as diverse post-human intelligences across thousands of star systems, or we are extinct, leaving the galaxy silent."
}
